    "title": "When is the WBC final? Schedule, how to watch USA vs Italy or Venezuela",
    "text": "March 16, 2026, 2:54 p.m. ETThe World Baseball Classic is nearly finished, and despite an underperforming offense, the United States will be playing in the championship game. After defeating the Dominican Republic 2-1 in the semis, the U.S. will face the winner of tonight's Italy vs. Venezuela game for the 2026 title.Italy has yet to lose a game this tournament, and even defeated the United States 8-6 in pool play. The U.S. would obviously love a second opportunity to take them down, but Venezuela boasts no slouches either. Not only is their roster brimming with MLB talent, but they defeated previously undefeated Japan in the quarterfinals, proving themselves a serious contender for a WBC title.Regardless of who the United States will face in the title game, fans are sure to be intrigued by the matchup. This year's World Baseball Classic has drawn more viewers than any in years past. So, a U.S. win would certainly be icing on the cake.Here's when and where the championship game will happen and how you can watch it at home.When is the World Baseball Classic title game?The championship game will take place Tuesday, March 17 at 8 p.m. ET from loanDepot Park in Miami, Florida.How to watch the WBC championshipThe WBC championship game can be watched on FOX or streamed with services like Fubo, Hulu + Live TV, or YouTube TV.Stream the World Baseball Classic Final with FuboU.S. path to championship gamePool PlayFriday, March 6United States 15, Brazil 5Saturday, March 7United States 9, Great Britain 1Monday, March 9United States 5, Mexico 3Tuesday, March 10Italy 8, United States 6QuarterfinalsFriday, March 13United States 5, Canada 3SemifinalsSunday, March 14United States 2, Dominican Republic 1Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
